---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/home.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Herm Greider — Portfolio">

  <main class="below-fold">

    <section class="project-detail bio-section">
      <div class="project-media headshot-container">
        <img src="/images/bio_herm.jpg" alt="Herm Greider" class="headshot" />
      </div>
      <div class="project-text">
        <h1>Herm Greider</h1>
        <div class="cv-summary">
          <p><strong>Software Developer</strong></p>
          <p>
            Retired Software Developer with 40 years experience leading, designing, and coding all types of software
            systems for defense and commercial applications. 
          </p>
          <p>
            Current projects include building LED and sound installations
          </p>
          <ul class="cv-details">
            <li><strong>Education:</strong> BS Computer Science, UC. MS CS Wright State</li>
            <li><strong>Expertise:</strong> Lighting and Sound Installations, Software Development</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="social-links">
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hermgreider" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="social-item">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M19 0h-14c-2.761 0-5 2.239-5 5v14c0 2.761 2.239 5 5 5h14c2.762 0 5-2.239 5-5v-14c0-2.761-2.238-5-5-5zm-11 19h-3v-11h3v11zm-1.5-12.268c-.966 0-1.75-.79-1.75-1.764s.784-1.764 1.75-1.764 1.75.79 1.75 1.764-.783 1.764-1.75 1.764zm13.5 12.268h-3v-5.604c0-3.368-4-3.113-4 0v5.604h-3v-11h3v1.765c1.396-2.586 7-2.777 7 2.476v6.759z"/></svg>
              LinkedIn
            </a>
            <a href="https://www.instagram.com/hermgreider" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="social-item">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2.163c3.204 0 3.584.012 4.85.07 3.252.148 4.771 1.691 4.919 4.919.058 1.265.069 1.645.069 4.849 0 3.205-.012 3.584-.069 4.849-.149 3.225-1.664 4.771-4.919 4.919-1.266.058-1.644.07-4.85.07-3.204 0-3.584-.012-4.849-.07-3.26-.149-4.771-1.699-4.919-4.92-.058-1.265-.07-1.644-.07-4.849 0-3.204.013-3.583.07-4.849.149-3.227 1.664-4.771 4.919-4.919 1.266-.057 1.645-.069 4.849-.069zm0-2.163c-3.259 0-3.667.014-4.947.072-4.358.2-6.78 2.618-6.98 6.98-.059 1.281-.073 1.689-.073 4.948 0 3.259.014 3.668.072 4.948.2 4.358 2.618 6.78 6.98 6.98 1.281.058 1.689.072 4.948.072 3.259 0 3.668-.014 4.948-.072 4.354-.2 6.782-2.618 6.979-6.98.059-1.28.073-1.689.073-4.948 0-3.259-.014-3.667-.072-4.947-.196-4.354-2.617-6.78-6.979-6.98-1.281-.058-1.69-.072-4.949-.072zm0 5.838c-3.403 0-6.162 2.759-6.162 6.162s2.759 6.163 6.162 6.163 6.162-2.759 6.162-6.163-2.759-6.162-6.162-6.162zm0 10.162c-2.209 0-4-1.79-4-4 0-2.209 1.791-4 4-4s4 1.791 4 4c0 2.21-1.791 4-4 4zm6.406-11.845c-.796 0-1.441.645-1.441 1.44s.645 1.44 1.441 1.44c.795 0 1.439-.645 1.439-1.44s-.644-1.44-1.439-1.44z"/></svg>
              Instagram
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-text">
        <h2>Cincinnati Nature Center Light in the Forest</h2>
        <p>Created lighting and sound installation for Cincinnati Nature Center's 2025 Light in the Forest event. 
          Microcontroller programming, music synthesizer programming, electronics design.          
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-media gallery-grid">
        <img src="/images/cnc_install.jpg" alt="Light In Forest 1">
        <img src="/images/board3.jpg" alt="Light In Forest 2">
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-text">
        <h2>Ceramic Lamp with Programmable LEDs</h2>
        <p>This piece was the result of a collaboration with ceramic artist <a href="http://rachel.greider.org">Rachel
           Greider</a>. Designed as an eye-catching centerpiece, the ceramic lamp casts vibrant shadows across the ceiling. 
           It served as a direct precursor to our <i>Light Portals</i> project — an essential prototype for exploring the 
           mathematical algorithms involved in arranging LEDs.       
        </p>
        <p>
          The LED rig features a custom circuit board, programmed algorithms for a microcontroller, and a seamless integration
          with the ceramic lamp form.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-media gallery-grid">
        <video controls="controls" preload="metadata" class="singlevideo">
          <source src="/images/herm/lamp-insta.mp4#t=0.1">
        </video>
        <video controls="controls" preload="metadata" class="singlevideo">
          <source src="/images/herm/lamp-prog1.mp4#t=0.1">
        </video>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-text">
        <h2>Homemade Music Synthesizer (in cardboard box)</h2>
        <p>
          As a longtime keyboard player and programmer, I was interested in combining the two worlds. This
          prototype explores the potential of connecting a synthesizer with real time user interaction through a DIY circuit
          board with keyboard input and external sensors.
        </p>
        <p>
          For this demo, instead of pre-programming a song, I've rigged it to take input from a Yamaha keyboard paired with a
          simple UI to tweak parameters like a traditional synth.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the core of the project is the Daisy Seed. A programmable audio hardware unit designed for real time audio processing.
          It makes it easy to incorporate external sensors — like proximity or touch inputs — for dynamic sound
          modulation. It was also a fun excuse to revisit my soldering skills and build a custom circuit board to handle MIDI
          input and signal processing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-media gallery-grid">
        <img src="/images/herm/synth-keyboard.jpg" alt="Synth 1">
        <img src="/images/herm/synth-assembly.jpg" alt="Synth 2">
        <img src="/images/herm/synth-ui.jpg" alt="Synth 2">
      </div>
      <div class="project-media gallery-grid">
        <video controls="controls" preload="metadata" class="singlevideo">
          <source src="/images/herm/synth-sound.mp4#t=0.1">
        </video>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  /* Use is:global to override the flex alignment of .project-detail for this specific section */
  
  /* Select the first project-detail (the bio section) */
  .below-fold > section.project-detail:first-of-type {
    align-items: flex-start; /* Aligns both text and image to the top */
    padding-top: 2rem;       /* Reduced padding at the top of the page */
  }

  /* Target the container for Aaron's image */
  .headshot-container {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-start; /* Align image to the left of its container */
    margin-top: 1rem;            /* Slight gap from the very top border */
    flex: 0 0 auto;              /* Prevents the image container from growing/shrinking weirdly */
  }
  
  /* The actual image constraints */
  .headshot {
    width: 150px !important;     /* Much smaller diameter (reduced from 250px) */
    height: 150px !important;    /* Must match width for the circle shape */
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 50%;         /* Maintains the circular headshot */
    border: 3px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); /* Subtle border */
    box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);      /* Adds some depth */
  }

  /* Ensure the text block stays readable and aligned */
  .below-fold > section.project-detail:first-of-type .project-text {
    flex: 1; /* Allows text to take available space */
    padding-right: 2rem; /* Gap between text and image */
  }

  /* Responsive adjustment for mobile screens */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .below-fold > section.project-detail:first-of-type {
      flex-direction: column-reverse; /* Stacks image above text on mobile */
      align-items: center;            /* Center aligns elements on mobile */
      text-align: center;
    }

    .headshot-container {
      justify-content: center;
      margin-top: 0;
      margin-bottom: 1rem; /* Gap between image and text when stacked */
    }

    .cv-details {
      display: inline-block; /* Helps center the list on mobile */
      text-align: left;
    }
  }

  /* Keep the rest of the standardized gallery/video styles you had */
  .cv-summary p {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cv-details {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .cv-details li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #ccc;
  }

  .social-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .social-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .social-item:hover {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .social-item svg {
    fill: #ccc; /* Subtle icon color */
  }

  .gallery-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .gallery-grid img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 400px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .video-wrapper {
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: 56.25%;
    height: 0;
  }

  .video-wrapper iframe {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>